   checkout and local AGENTS. A summaries-only source audit is not a source audit.
   Do not reread every specialist file for an unrelated small task, or create an
   endless orientation project. Deep implementation stays with owners; the root
   must understand the contracts it accepts and resolve contradictions itself.

4. Check live agents and current captain evidence BEFORE spawning/restarting work.
   Existing running owners continue across root compaction. Verify actual source
   revision, build/process/queue, immutable binaries and receiving status. Keep
   authored / compiled / executed / integrated / deployed claims distinct. Never
   duplicate an active native build because a stale note said it was not started.
   Read INTEGRATION plus captain's newest message: either can lag the other.
   Audit work/integration-obligations against fresh stopped/running agents.
   Verify diagnostic/dependency readiness, then followup_task stopped owners whose
